SkillForge — Stateless AI skill runtime at http://localhost:9147

Start: docker compose up -d
Health: GET /health → {"status":"healthy","skills_loaded":51}

Use skills:
  GET  /api/skills                 — list all (filter: ?category=data, ?search=csv)
  GET  /api/skills/{id}/info       — read schema BEFORE calling
  POST /api/skills/{id}/run        — execute with {"data": {...}}

Response format (always):
  {"success": true/false, "data": {...}, "error": "", "metadata": {...}}

Worker contract (immutable):
  class Worker(BaseWorker):
      skill_id = "category.skill-name"
      def run(self, input: SkillInput) -> SkillOutput: ...

Rules:
  - No database, no global state, no print()
  - Never raise — return SkillOutput(success=False, error="...")
  - Type hints on every function, docstrings on every class
  - schema.json first, then worker.py, SKILL.md, test.py (min 3 tests)
  - All dev on 'dev' branch, never push directly to 'master'

See AGENTS.md for full reference.

